# The app's published ComponentHost types — downloaded, never committed.
# README.md has the command. They describe the host that is deployed, so a copy
# pinned in git would be a snapshot of a contract that keeps moving.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, all of these: an unanchored `types/` would also
# swallow `src/types/`, so a perfectly ordinary source directory of that name
# would go unpushed and the build would fail on a file that exists on your disk.
/types/

# Editor-only tooling. The build refuses a repo that DECLARES dependencies (any
# of the four fields), so anything installed to make an editor happy has to stay
# uncommitted. A dependency-free package.json is legal — un-ignore it if you
# have a reason to commit one.
/node_modules/
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/pnpm-lock.yaml
/yarn.lock
